  castSubtitle: 'London to London — the four people who circumnavigate the globe in eighty days.',
  castLead: `<p>Around the World in Eighty Days has an unusually small named cast for a globe-spanning adventure: the four principals and a handful of significant supporting figures at specific stops. The smallness is deliberate — Verne is not writing a novel of society but a novel of mechanism, and the mechanism requires a few precisely calibrated figures rather than a crowd.</p>`,
